notes = "(!) Firmware lives at <save>/EKA2L1/ — populate it with the standalone EKA2L1 (desktop / Android) OR call retro_eka2l1_install_rom_ex / retro_eka2l1_install_game at runtime via the custom extension API (see libretro_eka2l1.h).|(!) Content path: .sis/.sisx/.n-gage (install+run package; .n-gage = N-Gage 2.0 on S60v3+), a folder (original N-Gage 1.0 game-card dump with system/apps/), 'ngage:/abs/folder', or 'uid:0xXXXXXXXX' (launch installed app).|(!) CPU backend: dyncom (interpreter) is the default, dynarmic JIT requires iOS 26+ with StikDebug."

description = "Port of the EKA2L1 Symbian OS / N-Gage emulator to libretro. Exposes a Symbian-specific extension surface (retro_eka2l1_*) so a custom RetroArch frontend can enumerate installed devices and apps, install ROM/RPKG/SIS images, and launch apps by UID — matching what the EKA2L1 Android client offers. Standard libretro callbacks handle HW OpenGLES3 video, audio_batch and RetroPad input."
